Two issues: (1) Images with extensive EXIF metadata were hitting the 32KB buffer limit in dimension reading, causing "Corrupt JPG, exceeded buffer limits" errors. (2) Served image paths were not logged at info level.

## Changes

- **Increased image header buffer from 32KB to 512KB** (`src/imageScanner.ts`)
  - Handles JPEGs with large EXIF data and progressive encoding
  - Extracted as `IMAGE_HEADER_BUFFER_SIZE` constant for maintainability

- **Log full image paths at info level** (`src/index.ts`)
  - Changed from `logger.debug(basename)` to `logger.info(fullPath)`
  - Output: `Serving image: /images/2024/Paris, Zermatt & Chamonix/DSC08915.jpg`

```typescript
// Before
const buffer = Buffer.alloc(32768);
logger.debug(`Serving image: ${path.basename(randomImage)}`);

// After
const IMAGE_HEADER_BUFFER_SIZE = 524288; // 512KB
const buffer = Buffer.alloc(IMAGE_HEADER_BUFFER_SIZE);
logger.info(`Serving image: ${randomImage}`);
```

